```

## Tutorials

Go through each character and count how many are digits (0-9).

Explanation:We loop through each character of the string. The methodCharacter.isDigit()checks if the character is a digit. For the example above, the program finds 5 digits.

### Code Examples

```
Example
String text = "W3Schools was founded in 1998";
int count = 0;

for (char c : text.toCharArray()) {
  if (Character.isDigit(c)) {
    count++;
  }
}

System.out.println("Digits: " + count);
